# Google Sheets service account, for writing waitlist signups to a Sheet
# instead of local disk/git. Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and
# fill in real values there, never here, this file is committed to git.
#
# See the README for how to obtain each of these:
#   - GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL / GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY come
#     from a Google Cloud service account's downloaded JSON key.
#   - WAITLIST_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID and SURVEY_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID are the ids in each
#     Sheet's own URL, between /d/ and /edit. Two separate sheets, two
#     separate purposes, never point both at the same one:
#       - WAITLIST_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID: a dedicated, empty sheet this app writes
#         signups into. Shared with the service account as Editor.
#       - SURVEY_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID: the Typeform-linked survey responses
#         sheet, this app only ever reads from it. Shared with the service
#         account as Viewer only, never Editor.

# The service account's own email.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=

# The service account's private key from its downloaded JSON key file.
# Paste it with literal \n for newlines if your tooling needs a single line,
# the app un-escapes those back into real newlines when reading it.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Dedicated waitlist-signups sheet, this app writes to it. Editor access.
# WAITLIST_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=

# Typeform-linked survey responses sheet, this app only reads it. Viewer
# access only, never share this one as Editor.
# SURVEY_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=

# Which tab in the waitlist sheet to write to. Optional, defaults to "Test"
# locally and "Live" in a production build (NODE_ENV=production), so a
# local test run can never land next to real signups. Set this explicitly
# for a Netlify deploy preview/branch deploy, those still build in
# production mode but shouldn't write real signups either, e.g. set it to
# "Test" for any non-production Netlify context.
# WAITLIST_SHEET_TAB=
